# Hash-locked scanners for the CI security-scan workflow ONLY.
#
# Scorecard's PinnedDependenciesID flagged `pipCommand not pinned by
# hash`, and requirements-lint.in already carries that note -- but three
# scanners were still installed with floors:
#
#     pip install "bandit>=1.7"
#     pip install "semgrep>=1.170"
#     pip install "pip-audit>=2.7"
#
# A security scan that resolves its own scanner from an unpinned range
# is deciding what counts as secure using code nobody reviewed. These
# are the tools whose verdict gates a release, so they are the last
# place to accept "whatever PyPI served this minute".
#
# Regenerate: uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --strip-extras \
#   --output-file=requirements-security.lock requirements-security.in
bandit==1.9.2
pip-audit==2.9.0
semgrep==1.145.0
